EXTERNAL chose(knot)

// [draft]
=== lana_corner ===
Hello. I'm Lana, Nawal's daughter. I've just come from the hotel, and I've brought the papers. #lana #neutral
Lana?! The last time I saw you, you were eight… I've made you a corner for your things. #salma #surprised
Good, thanks. And I'll need a copy of every invoice, so we can talk about selling. #lana
Selling? This isn't a meeting, Lana… you haven't even had a cup yet! #salma
Work before coffee. Right, where's the corner? #lana
-> END

// [draft]
=== tea_shelf ===
No, no, that's not how it's done. Tea needs mint, it has to steep slowly, and everyone sugars their own glass. #lana
Mint? We use sage, and the sugar goes in the pot from the start. That's how Teta made it. #salma
Sage? In [[shahi]]? What kind of story is that? #lana #surprised
Shahi? It's called [[shai]], Lana. Shai. #salma #smile
Shahi. End of discussion. #lana
-> END

// [draft]
=== shared_ledger ===
We split the ledger down the middle: a line through every page. The right side's yours, the left is mine. #lana
Why do I get the right? #salma #thinking
Arabic starts on the right, and you're the older one. See? I'm being fair. #lana
So what are we now, partners or neighbours? #salma
Neighbours. Until we sell. #lana #neutral
-> END

// [draft]
=== lanterns ===
Well, I never… Cardamom and Sugar, under one lantern! #abu_fadi #smile
What did you say, Uncle? #lana #surprised
That's what your Teta called you. Salma was Cardamom: you smelled her before you saw her. Lana was Sugar: she melted at the first tear. #abu_fadi
Lana? Sugar? #salma #smile
Don't laugh. I was sugar, Uncle. Now I'm black coffee. #lana
-> END

// [draft]
=== back_room_door ===
This door is sulking. The wood's swollen, and no one's opened it in years. #karim
Why did my grandmother keep it locked? #lana #thinking
The [[Hajja]] told me once: this room has its time. Looks like its time has come. #karim
Easy now, my friend… there. It's open. #karim
It smells of cardamom and old paper… it smells like Teta. #salma #sad
-> END

// [draft]
=== back_room ===
Salma, come here. Look what I found… our drawing! #lana #surprised
Eid 2005! Teta behind the counter, the two of us beside her, and each of us wrote her own name. #salma #smile
And you coloured outside the lines, and I sulked for three hours. #lana
Two. And then Teta cut a piece of knafeh down the middle for us. #salma
Down the middle… like the ledger. #lana #sad
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_lead ===
This room… when the café was at its busiest, she'd slip in here and come out with her arms full. #abu_fadi
And every night, before she closed, she locked the tin box. #abu_fadi
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_intro ===
Um Khalil! The café's overflowing, and the lads want ten cups. #fadi_young
Coming, Mr. Fadi! The cups, the tray, the big dallah… where did I put them? #teta_young
Come on, hands, search. A guest won't wait, and cardamom won't grind itself. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_perfect ===
Not a minute lost! Work done right does you credit. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_ok ===
We're a little late… but a guest who waits gets the better coffee. #teta_young
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_outro ===
What do you keep in that tin box, Um Khalil? Gold? #fadi_young #smile
The first coin this café ever earned. That one never gets spent, not even on the hardest day. #teta_young
She locked the box and hid the key behind the clock. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m3_return ===
The clock… every night, before she closed, she'd reach behind it. #abu_fadi
There's a key! And in the box there's an old coin… and an envelope that says: Salma. #lana #surprised
For me? #salma #surprised
-> END

// [draft]
=== letter_2 ===
To Salma, my little cardamom, #letter
When your mother was seven, she climbed onto the roof to fetch the boys' ball, came down with a scraped knee, and didn't cry. #letter
She was stubborn, like me. Once she said no, the whole world couldn't turn her. #letter
When everyone left, she stayed. She stayed in Amman, and she stayed by me, even when she stopped coming through the café's door. #letter
That isn't her fault, my heart. It's mine. #letter
She only knows half the story… #letter_faded
Don't be hurt by her stubbornness. In her, stubbornness is love that hasn't found its way yet. #letter
— Your Teta #letter_signature
-> END

// [draft]
=== voice_2 ===
Salma, my heart… your mother is as headstrong as I am. Don't wait for her to come. Go to her, and take a cup with you. #teta
-> END

// [draft]
=== notify_2 ===
Salma, Samira tells me your cousin has arrived. Take care of yourself… and don't stay late at your Teta's café. #rana
-> END
